    <string name="billiard_lesson_clear">Use the dial to line up the ball and pocket. Adjust power, then shoot. Start gently: potting does not require maximum power.</string>
    <string name="billiard_lesson_bank">Aim so the object ball hits a cushion before falling into a pocket. Imagine the pocket reflected across the cushion; refine with the aiming guide.</string>
    <string name="billiard_lesson_order">Hit and pot the lowest numbered ball first. Think about where the white will stop for the next shot.</string>
    <string name="billiard_lesson_draw">Open the effects panel and hit below the centre. Pot the ball and bring the white back into the marked zone. Close the panel by tapping outside.</string>
    <string name="billiard_lesson_follow">Open the effects panel and hit above the centre. Pot the ball and send the white forward into the marked zone.</string>
    <string name="billiard_lesson_carom">The white must touch both other balls in the same stroke. Start with a soft shot and follow its path.</string>
    <string name="billiard_objective_clear">Pot %1$d balls in at most %2$d shots.</string>
    <string name="billiard_objective_bank">Pot the target after it touches a cushion. %2$d shots maximum.</string>
    <string name="billiard_objective_order">Pot %1$d balls in numerical order. %2$d shots maximum.</string>
    <string name="billiard_objective_draw">Pot the target with backspin and stop the white in the zone. %2$d attempts.</string>
    <string name="billiard_objective_follow">Pot the target with topspin and stop the white in the zone. %2$d attempts.</string>
    <string name="billiard_objective_carom">Touch both balls, with at least %1$d cushions before the second. %2$d attempts.</string>
